  "limitations": [
    "No explicit limitations of the proposed hybrid method were stated in the paper. The paper focuses on addressing the limitations of existing methods (Isomap and CDA) regarding false colors and continuity errors."
  ],
  "minimum_safe_summary": "This paper proposes a new hybrid dimensionality reduction method for visualizing medical image datasets, combining continuity (Isomap) and trustworthiness (curvilinear distance analysis - CDA) properties. The method aims to overcome the problem of 'false colors' and continuity errors present in existing visualization techniques, which can lead to incorrect analysis by specialists. Experimental results demonstrate that the hybrid method produces a better visualization by more accurately preserving color distances between the visualization and original high-dimensional data, resulting in fewer false colors and a more trustworthy representation compared to Isomap and CDA. The paper does not explicitly state limitations of the proposed method, but rather highlights its success in addressing the shortcomings of previous approaches.",
